Code Ownership
Proprietary lock-in / maintenance traps
100% Source Code Ownership










  2. The Kode Company Next.js 15 Blueprint


When architecting web platforms — whether it is a client business site or our flagship SaaS platform KodeCRM — we follow three architectural rules:




  A. Zero Client-Side Data Fetching on Route Entry (RSC First)


Instead of wrapping pages in useEffect() or heavy client-side state bundles, we use React Server Components (RSC) to fetch and stream content directly from the edge.





typescript
// app/services/page.tsx - Clean Server Component Architecture
import { Suspense } from "react";
import { ServiceGrid } from "@/components/services/ServiceGrid";
import { ServiceSkeleton } from "@/components/services/ServiceSkeleton";

export const revalidate = 3600; // ISR cache at the edge for 1 hour

export default async function ServicesPage() {
  return (
    &lt;main className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-20"&gt;
      &lt;header className="mb-12"&gt;
        &lt;h1 className="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white"&gt;
          Enterprise Solutions &amp; Technical Consulting
        &lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;p className="text-zinc-400 mt-2"&gt;
          Sub-second digital platforms engineered in Trivandrum, deployed globally.
        &lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;/header&gt;

      {/* Instant TTFB with Streaming SSR */}
      &lt;Suspense fallback={&lt;ServiceSkeleton /&gt;}&gt;
        &lt;ServiceGrid /&gt;
      &lt;/Suspense&gt;
    &lt;/main&gt;
  );
}
